     aaccppii__rraappiiddssttaarrtt — Intel rapid start technology ACPI driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aaccppii__rraappiiddssttaarrtt

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           acpi_rapidstart_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccppii__rraappiiddssttaarrtt driver provides support for Intel Rapid Start tech‐
     nology ACPI device interface.  Note that this is only for the ACPI device
     interface.  This has _CID PNP0C02 so it should be loaded at boot time to
     avoid attaching to the acpi_sysresource driver.

